              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A piecewise-defined function is always discontinuous where the formula changes. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 17
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. In the worked example, the branches $-x$ and $x^2$ meet at $x=-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-1)&=(-1)^2=1\\\\f_L(-1)&=-(-1)=1\\\\f_R(-1)&=(-1)^2=1\\end{align*}$$\nAll three values agree, so the function is continuous there even though its formula changes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p114-ex2l-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p114-ex2l-q1-b-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "If ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "f_L(2)=f_R(2)",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", then ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "f",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is continuous when ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "x=2",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "False",
                  "width": 17
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. The value $f(2)$ must also be defined and equal both approached values. Continuity requires\n$$f_L(2)=f(2)=f_R(2).$$\nEquality of the two approached values alone does not establish this.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
