          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. For example, let\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}0&\\text{if }x<2,\\\\1&\\text{if }x\\geq2.\\end{cases}$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{align*}f(2)&=1\\\\f_L(2)&=0\\\\f_R(2)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe three values do not all agree, so the function is discontinuous at $x=2$, although $f(2)$ is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p114-ex2l-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p114-ex2l-q1-e-statement",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Two different piecewise definitions can describe exactly the same function. ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "cloze",
                  "answer": "True",
                  "width": 17
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "True. In the worked example, the branches $-x$ and $x^2$ both give $1$ at $x=-1$. Assigning this boundary point to either branch, with all other rules unchanged, gives the same output for every input. The two piecewise definitions therefore describe the same function.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      }
